{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST resolve its saved configuration before constructing Rig provider\nclients and completion models. The Habeas data structures MUST remain the saved\nformat. Rig model references MAY be reused internally without discarding the\nconnection settings they do not represent.\n\nThe Bedrock adapter MUST pass the chosen AWS profile and region through AWS SDK\nconfiguration, or use explicitly configured credentials. The Ollama adapter MUST use the chosen server, exact model ID,\nand optional authentication; the server MAY be local or remote. Both adapters\nMUST supply the same tools and initial prompt.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The mapping itself is implemented and well tested. The gap is that some code implementing parts of the requirement is not marked `{impl}` for it. I did not run the tests; this judgment is from reading the sources.\n\n**What is implemented and marked**\n- `configured_record` and `configured_assessment` (src/authoring/mod.rs) resolve the saved config via `config::resolve_authoring` before calling `RigProvider::connect`. The saved `BackendConfig`, `BedrockConfig` and `OllamaConfig` structures stay the stored format.\n- `RigProvider::connect` (src/authoring/providers.rs:79) builds the Rig clients.\n  - Bedrock uses `bedrock_sdk_config`, which passes `aws_profile`, `region` and explicit credentials through the AWS SDK loader.\n  - Ollama uses `with_base_url(config.endpoint())`, the optional `api_key`, and `native_completion(&config.model)` with the exact model ID.\n- `complete`, `apply_bedrock_options`, `options_json` and `normalize_bedrock_client_calls` are marked `{impl}`. They map saved options onto Rig requests without discarding the settings Rig does not model.\n- `Rig` model references are reused internally through `erase()`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `explicit_bedrock_credentials_reach_the_sdk_without_the_default_chain` checks explicit credentials and region reach the SDK.\n- `bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools` checks profile credentials, region and inference options, and the same six tools and prompt. It runs both untyped and typed tool-call responses.\n- `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` checks the chosen model, options, bearer auth, the same six tools and the prompt content.\n- `authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file` checks a workspace-selected Ollama config with a remote endpoint.\n- Unit tests cover Bedrock option typing and the tool-call normalization.\n\n**Gaps**\n1. The obligation \"Both adapters MUST supply the same tools and initial prompt\" is implemented in `assess` (building `CompletionRequest::new(initial_prompt(..))` with `request.tools = tool_definitions()?`) and in `tool_definitions`. Neither is marked `{impl}` for `rig_configuration_mapping`. Both carry `{impl}` marks for other requirements only (`initial_prompt`, `submission`, and others). The tests do verify this obligation, but the implementation is not attributed to it.\n2. `OllamaConfig::endpoint`, `OllamaConfig::api_key` and `OllamaConfig::api_key_from` (src/config.rs:509-540) implement the Ollama \"chosen server … and optional authentication\" part. They are marked only for `configuration_precedence`, `credentials` and `serialization`, not for this requirement. The `BackendConfig::model_ref` helper is marked only for `configuration_structure`.\n3. I found no test for an Ollama config with no authentication, where no Authorization header should be sent. I found no test for a default or local endpoint either.\n\nBecause part of the implementation is not marked, and nothing in the source acknowledges this with a FIXME, the subject is not fully satisfied.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.rig_configuration_mapping",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.rig_configuration_mapping"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} rig_configuration_mapping",
        "Habeas MUST resolve its saved configuration before constructing Rig provider",
        "clients and completion models. The Habeas data structures MUST remain the saved",
        "format. Rig model references MAY be reused internally without discarding the",
        "connection settings they do not represent.",
        "",
        "The Bedrock adapter MUST pass the chosen AWS profile and region through AWS SDK",
        "configuration, or use explicitly configured credentials. The Ollama adapter MUST use the chosen server, exact model ID,",
        "and optional authentication; the server MAY be local or remote. Both adapters",
        "MUST supply the same tools and initial prompt.",
        ":::"
      ]
